  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Jonny On The Spot** (1 review): Played as \"I'll Be Your Johnny On The Spot\" and segues directly into the next song, LA Woman [2]\n- **LA Woman** (1 review): A cover of The Doors, reached by segue from Johnny On The Spot, just before Ocean Man [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Jonny On The Spot**: back after 124 archived shows (3669 days) [3]\n- **LA Woman**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Stallion Pt. 2**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Stallion Pt 4**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2018-07-25.FLAC.16bit** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 141 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- After Someday, the encore consisted of all five parts of Stallion, played in order [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2018-07-25.FLAC.16bit**: taped by Peter Retzlaff; transferred by Peter Retzlaff; source: H4N [1]",
